    {"assumption": "Output-extraction red-teaming produces a stable, measurable extraction rate (records regenerable per N prompts) that holds across the prompt distribution an attacker would actually use, not just the red-team's sampled prompts.", "if_wrong": "If the measured extraction curve does not generalize to adversarial prompts the red-team never tried, the actuarial input is biased low and the reserve underprices the tail — degrading the regime toward after-the-fact litigation, which is the Skeptic's exact prediction."},
    {"assumption": "A public board can hold appointment-and-tenure authority over the red-team auditors independently of the premium-paying firms, the way the PCAOB holds it over issuer-paid audits.", "if_wrong": "If the board is captured or underfunded the way PCAOB inspection cadence has lagged, supervisory independence erodes and the watchdog's paycheck conflict re-emerges at the board level."}
